upstream: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cloudflare/skills/main/skills/cloudflare
verified: 2026-09-29
scope: directory
reason: Two deliberate local lines; everything else is byte-identical to upstream (last path commit 320fbbc1).
  (1) Frontmatter description. Upstream's reads "Discover and choose Cloudflare products ..." with no
  boundary. Codex keeps only ~240 characters of each description once many skills are installed
  (see skill-check CODEX_DESCRIPTION_CUT), so the what AND the sibling boundary must be front-loaded:
  local puts the "Not for sibling-owned work: workers-best-practices, wrangler, durable-objects,
  agents-sdk, sandbox-*, cloudflare-one*, email" clause inside the first 238 characters, then a
  sibling map (adds sandbox-migrate-to-next and cloudflare-one-migrations, vendored 2026-09-29) and
  the product terms users type (KV, R2, Tunnel, WAF, Terraform, Pulumi ...). This is AUDIT-H-04's
  routing fix carried forward. Upstream also dropped the old "references:" frontmatter key; local
  follows upstream there.
  (2) SKILL.md need-to-product table, Next.js row: upstream links ../nextjs-on-cloudflare/SKILL.md,
  a sibling skill that is not vendored in this dotfiles tree, so skill-check fails it as a broken
  relative link. Local points the same link text at
  https://github.com/cloudflare/skills/tree/main/skills/nextjs-on-cloudflare instead.
would_lose_if_wired: a byte-for-byte refresh would drop the front-loaded sibling boundary (Codex
  would route every Cloudflare task here) and reintroduce a broken relative link.
refresh_guard: _refresh-vendored.sh skips this directory when .local-fork is present, before any
  fetch or write. To re-sync: fetch upstream into a scratch dir, rsync --delete over this dir
  excluding .local-fork/.source, then re-apply (1) and (2) and diff against upstream.
to_vendor: (2) disappears if nextjs-on-cloudflare is vendored as a sibling (restore upstream's
  relative link). (1) stays unless upstream adopts an equivalent front-loaded boundary.
history: 2026-08-16 fork (description-only, sandbox-sdk -> sandbox-next/stable) and 2026-09-04
  TASK-049 trim are superseded by this re-sync; see git history for the earlier ledger text.
decision: 2026-09-29 — nextjs-on-cloudflare deliberately NOT vendored. Upstream's body is a
  redirect that tells the agent to run `npx skills add cloudflare/vinext`; on this machine the
  runtime skill dirs are symlinks into skills/local, so that installer would write third-party
  files into owned skills (same hazard as `playwright-cli install --skills -g`). Keep (2).
